    { label: "DMPX-028 (MOPX 207 / WHPX 407)", href: "/centrifuges/dmpx-028/" },
    { label: "DMPX-042 (four exact base-machine variants)", href: "/centrifuges/dmpx-042/" },
    { label: "DMB-062 Manual-Clean", href: "/centrifuges/dmb-062/" },
  ]}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  hideBottomCTA={true}
>

  <article class="prose-dolphin max-w-none">

    <p>
      The DMPX-070 is a Dolphin-engineered turnkey module class supplied with a remanufactured Alfa Laval MOPX 213 or WHPX 513 centrifuge. These are distinct base machines with different published capacity records, so every flow value remains attached to its exact machine and fluid. Dolphin is an independent remanufacturer and is not affiliated with or authorized by Alfa Laval.
    </p>

    <!-- Product Image -->
    <figure class="text-center my-8">
      <img
        src="/images/alfa-laval-whpx-513/WHPX-513_Waste_Oil_Centrifuge_UCO.webp"
        alt="Alfa Laval WHPX 513 self-cleaning disc stack centrifuge skid with motor, gearbox, and control panel, supplied by Dolphin as the DMPX-070 system"
        width="500"
        height="500"
        loading="lazy"
        class="rounded-lg shadow-lg img-cap-600 mx-auto"
      />
      <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2">
        DMPX-070 - Flagship Self-Cleaning 3-Phase Disc Stack Centrifuge (Alfa Laval WHPX 513 base machine)
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- Technical Specifications -->
    <h2 id="technical-specifications">Technical Specifications</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Parameter</th>
            <th>DMPX-070 Value</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Base-machine options</td><td>Alfa Laval MOPX 213 or WHPX 513 (remanufactured)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Diesel capacity, MOPX 213</td><td>14,400 L/h (63.40 US GPM derived), 40&deg;C, 13 cSt</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Marine-diesel capacity, WHPX 513</td><td>16,400 L/h (72.21 US GPM derived), 40&deg;C, 13 cSt</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513 rated reference</td><td>24,500 L/h (107.87 US GPM derived); source fluid unspecified, not a diesel or water capacity</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bowl Sludge Capacity</td><td>3.65–3.96 gallons</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bowl Speed</td><td>4,100–4,150 RPM</td></tr>
          <!-- TBD: Track-2 - DMPX-070 / WHPX 513 G-force figure still unresolved -->
          <tr><td>G-Force</td><td>7,000+</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Motor Power</td><td>15 HP</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Voltages</td><td>230 / 460 V, 3-Phase</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Separation Type</td><td>Three-phase (oil / water / solids)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Desludging</td><td>Automatic self-cleaning (hydraulic ejection)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Process</td><td>Continuous, unattended operation</td></tr>
          <tr><td>DMPX Series Position</td><td>Flagship / Largest (70 bowl equiv.)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-gold/10 border-l-4 border-gold rounded-r-xl p-5 my-8 not-prose">
      <p class="font-bold text-navy text-base mb-1">Need the complete datasheet?</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-light leading-relaxed mb-4">We'll email the complete datasheet - usually within one business day.</p>
      <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/" class="inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-semibold px-5 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-gold/90 transition-colors text-sm">Request the full spec sheet (PDF) -></a>
    </div>

    <!-- Capacity by Fluid Type -->
    <h2 id="capacity-by-fluid-type">Capacity by Fluid Type</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Exact base machine</th>
            <th>Fluid and source conditions</th>
            <th>Published capacity</th>
            <th>Derived capacity</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>MOPX 213</td><td>Gas oil at 40&deg;C</td><td>21,500 L/h</td><td>94.66 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>MOPX 213</td><td>Diesel, 13 cSt at 40&deg;C</td><td>14,400 L/h</td><td>63.40 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>MOPX 213</td><td>R&amp;O / engine lube oil, centrifuged at 80&ndash;90&deg;C</td><td>7,500 L/h</td><td>33.02 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>MOPX 213</td><td>Steam turbine lube oil, centrifuged at 60&ndash;70&deg;C</td><td>14,000 L/h</td><td>61.64 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>Rated reference; source fluid unspecified</td><td>24,500 L/h</td><td>107.87 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>Marine diesel, 13 cSt at 40&deg;C</td><td>16,400 L/h</td><td>72.21 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>HFO 30 cSt at 50&deg;C; centrifuged at 70&ndash;98&deg;C</td><td>15,200 L/h</td><td>66.92 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>HFO 40 cSt at 50&deg;C; centrifuged at 80&ndash;98&deg;C</td><td>15,200 L/h</td><td>66.92 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>HFO 60 cSt at 50&deg;C; centrifuged at 80&ndash;98&deg;C</td><td>11,500 L/h</td><td>50.63 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>HFO 100 cSt at 50&deg;C; centrifuged at 90&ndash;98&deg;C</td><td>11,000 L/h</td><td>48.43 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>HFO 180 cSt at 50&deg;C; centrifuged at 90&ndash;98&deg;C</td><td>7,600 L/h</td><td>33.46 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>HFO 380 cSt at 50&deg;C; centrifuged at 98&deg;C</td><td>6,400 L/h</td><td>28.18 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>HFO 460 cSt at 50&deg;C; centrifuged at 98&deg;C</td><td>5,400 L/h</td><td>23.78 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>HFO 600 cSt at 50&deg;C; centrifuged at 98&deg;C</td><td>4,400 L/h</td><td>19.37 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>Cross-head R&amp;O lube oil, centrifuged at 80&ndash;90&deg;C</td><td>7,400&ndash;8,600 L/h</td><td>32.58&ndash;37.86 US GPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WHPX 513</td><td>Steam turbine lube oil, centrifuged at 60&ndash;70&deg;C</td><td>15,900 L/h</td><td>70.01 US GPM</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">
      Source L/h values are canonical. US GPM is derived as L/h &divide; 227.124707 and rounded to two decimals. HFO values apply only to WHPX 513; none is transferred to MOPX 213. See the <a href="/technical-data/">technical-data methodology</a> and <a href="/technical-data/dolphin-dmpx-070.json">machine-readable DMPX-070 record</a>.
    </p>

    <InstallationRequirements />

    <!-- Key Applications -->
    <h2 id="key-applications">Key Applications</h2>

    <h3>Power Plant HFO &amp; Fuel Treatment</h3>
    <p>
      Large diesel and HFO-fired power plants require continuous <a href="/fuel-oil-centrifuge/">fuel purification</a>. On the WHPX 513 base machine, published HFO capacity is 15,200 L/h (66.92 US GPM derived) at 30 cSt and 6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM derived) at 380 cSt. Viscosity is specified at 50&deg;C; the 380 cSt centrifugation temperature is 98&deg;C. These are not MOPX 213 ratings.
    </p>

    <h3>Marine Vessel Fuel &amp; Oil Systems</h3>
    <p>
      On large commercial vessels, bulk carriers, tankers, and cruise ships, the DMPX-070 handles main-engine fuel and <a href="/lube-oil-centrifuge/">lube-oil</a> treatment. Published diesel values are 14,400 L/h (63.40 US GPM derived) for MOPX 213 and 16,400 L/h (72.21 US GPM) for WHPX 513. Lube-oil capacity remains tied to the exact oil category and base machine shown in the table.
    </p>

    <h3>Refinery Slop Oil Recovery</h3>
    <p>
      Refineries generate significant volumes of slop oil - mixed hydrocarbon streams contaminated with water and sediment. The DMPX-070 recovers this product-quality oil at high throughput, reducing refinery waste, improving yields, and minimizing environmental liability from contaminated oil disposal. See our <a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/">waste oil centrifuge</a> page for more on oil recovery applications.
    </p>

    <h3>Large-Volume Crude Oil BS&amp;W Reduction</h3>
    <p>
      For upstream production operations, gathering stations, and crude oil pipelines requiring BS&amp;W (basic sediment and water) reduction ahead of custody transfer or pipeline specification compliance, the DMPX-070 delivers the throughput needed to process high-volume crude streams continuously and without manual intervention.
    </p>

    <!-- Mid-Page CTA -->
    <div class="not-prose my-10 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-gold bg-gold/10 p-6 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-4">
      <div class="flex-1">
        <p class="text-navy font-bold text-lg mb-1">Specifying a DMPX-070 for your facility?</p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Our engineers handle power plant, refinery, and large marine specifications - including explosion-proof variants and custom skid packages.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/" class="shrink-0 inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gold/90 transition-colors text-center">
        Request a Quote &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- DMPX Series Comparison -->
    <h2 id="dmpx-series-comparison">The DMPX-070 as the Dolphin Series Flagship</h2>
    <p>
      The DMPX-070 is the largest model in the Dolphin DMPX range, delivering the highest throughput for the most demanding industrial applications. For applications requiring somewhat lower flow rates, the
      <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-042/">DMPX-042</a>
      provides a cost-effective alternative. Mid-range applications are served by the
      <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-028/">DMPX-028</a>, while compact installations use the
      <a href="/dmpx-014-self-cleaning-3-phase-disc-stack-centrifuge/">DMPX-014</a>
      or
      <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-010/">DMPX-010</a>. All DMPX classes use an automatic self-cleaning bowl design, but flow comparisons require the exact base machine, fluid, viscosity, and temperature.
      Visit our <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/">disc stack centrifuge overview</a> for a full model comparison, or <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/">contact us</a> for a sizing consultation.
    </p>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <h2 id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">What is the throughput of the DMPX-070 centrifuge?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        DMPX-070 is not one universal flow rating. Published diesel capacity is 14,400 L/h (63.40 US GPM derived) for MOPX 213 and 16,400 L/h (72.21 US GPM derived) for WHPX 513, both at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt. WHPX 513 separately lists a 24,500 L/h (107.87 US GPM) rated reference whose source fluid is unspecified.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">What is the DMPX-070 used for?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The DMPX-070 is used for large-scale power plant HFO and <a href="/diesel-centrifuge/">diesel</a> fuel treatment, marine vessel main engine fuel and lube oil purification, refinery slop oil recovery and crude oil dewatering, and high-volume industrial <a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/">waste oil</a> reclamation. Its 3.65–3.96-gallon sludge bowl supports continuous operation even with heavily contaminated streams.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">How large is the DMPX-070 sludge bowl?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The DMPX-070 features a 3.65–3.96-gallon sludge bowl - the largest in the Dolphin DMPX series. This large bowl capacity reduces ejection frequency and supports continuous operation even with high-solids streams such as crude oil tank bottoms, heavily contaminated <a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/">waste oil</a>, and high-ash HFO.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">What motor power does the DMPX-070 require?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The Dolphin DMPX-070 module specification calls for a 15 HP motor. Motor power does not establish a universal flow: capacity remains tied to the exact base machine, fluid, viscosity, and temperature. See the <a href="/technical-data/">technical-data registry</a> for the sourced records.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">How does the DMPX-070 compare to the DMPX-042?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Compare exact base machines. Published diesel values are 14,400 L/h (63.40 US GPM) for MOPX 213 and 16,400 L/h (72.21 US GPM) for WHPX 513, versus 7,900&ndash;10,700 L/h (34.78&ndash;47.11 US GPM) across the four exact <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-042/">DMPX-042</a> variants. <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/">Contact us</a> to size the selected machine for your fluid.
      </p>
    </details>

  </article>

